The '''2026 Sutton London Borough Council election''' will take place on 7 May 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-01 |title=Local elections in London will test support for Reform UK and Greens |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c99k0mzj7x8o |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> All 55 members of [[Sutton London Borough Council]] will be elected. The elections will take place alongside [[2026 London local elections|local elections in the other London boroughs]] and [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|elections to local authorities across the United Kingdom]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Number of councils that have requested delay to local elections revealed - is yours one of them? |url=https://news.sky.com/story/local-elections-2026-over-a-third-of-councils-offered-a-delay-have-requested-one-is-yours-on-the-list-13494762 |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=Sky News |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
In 2022, Liberal Democrats retained control of the council.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Sutton result - Local Elections 2022 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2022/england/councils/E09000029 |access-date=2026-01-19 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> In 2025, the deputy leader of the council resigned triggering a by-election.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Galliven |first=Harrison |date=2025-03-10 |title=By-election triggered after former Deputy Council Leader steps down |url=https://www.mylondon.news/news/south-london-news/south-london-election-triggered-after-31166388 |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=My London |language=en}}</ref>

